ritional, and lifestyle factors, and it poses a significant public health concern due to its impact on bone health and associated healthcare costs.\",83\r\n5716,BISFOSFONATOS,BISFOSFONATOS are medications used as an adjunct treatment for patients with celiac disease to prevent the loss of bone mineral density.,2\r\n3426,EJERCICIO FÍSICO REGULAR,\"\"\"EJERCICIO FÍSICO REGULAR\"\" refers to the practice of engaging in consistent physical activity, which is linked to numerous health benefits. It is particularly noted for its role in reducing the incidence of osteoporosis, a condition that weakens bones and increases the risk of fractures. Additionally, regular physical exercise is emphasized as a vital component for maintaining overall health and preventing diseases, especially in older adults. This highlights the importance of incorporating regular exercise into daily routines to promote longevity and enhance quality of life.\",2\r\n5094,GLUCOCORTICOIDS,\"Glucocorticoids are a class of steroid hormones that play a significant role in the regulation of metabolism and immune response. However, when used long-term or excessively, glucocorticoids can lead to osteoporosis, a condition characterized by weakened bones. This adverse effect occurs due to their impact on calcium absorption and bone formation, making individuals more susceptible to bone density loss. Additionally, resistance to glucocorticoids can result in various clinical conditions, highlighting the importance of careful management of these medications.\",2\r\n5702,ALENDRONATO,\"Alendronato, also known as Alendronate, is a bisphosphonate medication primarily used to treat osteoporosis. It is effective in reducing bone resorption and increasing bone mineral density, which helps to lower the risk of fractures in individuals with this condition.\",1\r\n11494,ANTIANDROGENS,Antiandrogens are medications that may increase the risk of osteoporosis.,1\r\n11496,ANTICONVULSANTS,Certain anticonvulsants are associated wi